<title>USA: Colo. issuer to appeal court ruling on Moody's.</title>
<headline>Colo. issuer to appeal court ruling on Moody's.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colorado's largest school district will appeal a U.S. judge's dismissal of federal antitrust and related state law claims it filed against Moody's Investors Service Inc, a lawyer for the school district said Tuesday.</p>
<p>Stuart Stuller, lawyer for Jefferson County School District, said that it took U.S. District Judge William Downes months to rule on motions by Moody's to dismiss the locality's 18-month-old lawsuit shows the case raised tough issues that need further review.</p>
</text>
